content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Flow: approximately 20% down over two weeks at unchanged valve settings. The only documented HF-300 flow reference is its rated duty of 300 m3/h at 45 m; this is not stated to be a minimum-flow, alarm or trip limit. The manual treats low flow or head as a troubleshooting symptom, but provides no allowable percentage flow loss. Actual baseline/current flow and head are therefore required for a quantitative comparison.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: 2.0 mm/s. Figure 3 is the applicable HF-300 severity chart only for vibration velocity in mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings. On that measurement basis, 2.0 is within Zone A (0.0–2.8), below the Zone B boundary at 2.8, Zone C restricted-operation range beginning at 4.5, and Zone D stop range beginning at 7.1. It does not trigger SSP-07's immediate-stop rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone. Classification is provisional because the report does not state RMS or measurement location.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature: 65 C. The applicable bearing-housing surface-temperature limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. Thus 65 C is within the documented normal range: 5 C below the normal upper value, 15 C below alarm and 25 C below trip. SSP-07's priority-1 requirement for bearing temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit is not triggered. Confirm that the reported reading is from the bearing-housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Leakage: none reported. The manual lists leakage at the shaft seal as a symptom requiring seal/alignment investigation, but gives no numerical allowable leakage limit. There is consequently no leak-rate limit comparison to make, and the absence of leakage does not by itself establish the internal condition of the seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "First investigate a worn impeller: it is a documented cause of low flow or head and fits the reported progressive performance loss. Inspect both the impeller and wear rings as directed; the report does not yet confirm that either is worn.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Second investigate air in the suction, another documented low-flow/head cause. Vent the casing and reassess before committing to internal replacement work.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Third verify that no valve is actually closed. A closed valve is a documented cause; unchanged valve settings make a recent setting change less likely, but do not verify the actual valve position.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before disassembly, record actual flow and head, verify suction/discharge valve positions, and vent the casing to address possible suction air. Reassess flow after these checks. Maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If low flow persists and internal inspection is required, isolate and drain the pump: apply electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanically isolate suction and discharge valves, obtain the line-break permit, and drain and vent before breaking containment.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly for access; it can be removed without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use the required signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment. Inspect the impeller and wear rings and record their condition; do not condemn parts without an applicable wear criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If inspection establishes that mechanical-seal replacement is necessary, follow procedure 5.2: remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, and inspect the sleeve. For this serial, do not fit HF3-450; fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B. No sleeve measurement is needed to set that seal, but the sleeve must still be inspected for scoring. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth, and fit a new casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, replace casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened. For disturbed Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, tighten casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm, impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm and bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm, as applicable. If HF3-450B is fitted, tighten its seal gland nuts to 30 Nm rather than the manual's superseded 25 Nm value.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the work moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment after reassembly. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reinstate the pump with seal flush available and verify flow/head, leakage, vibration and bearing-housing temperature. Compare recommissioning readings with the manufacturer's vibration zones and normal/alarm/trip temperature limits; stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart if vibration reaches highest-severity Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket, quantity one; required whenever the casing is opened for inspection or seal work.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal, quantity one, conditional on inspection establishing that seal replacement is required. This is the mandatory replacement for HF3-450 on serial HF3-22300; current symptoms alone do not authorise automatic seal replacement.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve, quantity one, conditional replacement only if the sleeve is withdrawn and scoring is found to exceed 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal, apply electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC, mechanically isolate both suction and discharge valves, and obtain a line-break permit; drain and vent before breaking containment.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The 68 kg back pull-out assembly exceeds SSP-07's 25 kg lifting threshold. Before lifting it, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If P-112 is confirmed to be on a chemically dosed line, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The supplied dosing note explicitly identifies P-101 to P-106, not P-112, so P-112's chemical service must be confirmed rather than assumed.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump dry during venting, testing or return to service.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration is subsequently measured in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. The reported 2.0 mm/s does not currently activate this control if confirmed on the Figure 3 RMS bearing-housing basis.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical-seal replacement allowance: 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. Include this allowance only if inspection converts the work to seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional laser-alignment allowance: 1.5 hours with 1 technician when the work moves the motor or bearing housing and alignment is therefore required.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part-number conflict: the manual parts list identifies component seal HF3-450, while Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits fitting HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and specifies HF3-450B. P-112 is serial HF3-22300 and therefore lies within the bulletin range. If a seal is replaced on this asset, use HF3-450B; the bulletin does not itself require proactive replacement of a serviceable seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque conflict: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B and explicitly identifies 25 Nm as the former value. For the HF3-450B replacement configuration on this serial, 30 Nm applies. Table 5 remains the source for the other listed fastener torques; pumps below HF3-22000 remain on HF3-450 and Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What are the actual baseline and current flow and head? The 20% reduction cannot be converted to m3/h or compared quantitatively with the rated 300 m3/h at 45 m without these values.",
    "Was the 2.0 mm/s vibration reading RMS and taken on a bearing housing, and is 65 C specifically the bearing-housing surface temperature? The documented severity and temperature classifications depend on those measurement bases.",
    "Do venting and verification of valve positions restore flow? This determines whether the back pull-out inspection and its associated lifting and containment controls are needed.",
    "What impeller or wear-ring wear is present, and what acceptance limits apply? The evidence supplies neither impeller/wear-ring wear limits nor a wear-ring part number, so their replacement scope cannot yet be fixed.",
    "Which seal is currently installed, and does inspection actually require seal or sleeve replacement? No leakage is reported, and the bulletin controls the replacement part and torque but does not establish present seal failure.",
    "Is P-112 exposed to any chemically dosed service? The supplied note identifies only P-101 to P-106 as sodium-hypochlorite-dosed; additional chemical controls cannot be decided from the evidence alone.",
    "Table 6 gives no labour standard for initial low-flow troubleshooting or impeller/wear-ring inspection, so the base inspection duration remains to be estimated after scope is known.",
    "The evidence defines a priority-1 trigger for bearing temperature above alarm but gives no P2/P3 definitions. P2 is therefore a planning judgement for material flow degradation without a current immediate-stop or temperature-P1 trigger."
  ]
}
